jobs.content:
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;3:1-3:52;82-133&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;On-site | Vancouver Office – &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;564 Beatty St&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About EviSmart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EviSmart builds the automation layer that dental laboratories run on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A dental lab is a manufacturing operation. A case arrives from a dentist — a 3D scan of a patient&#39;s mouth and a prescription — and leaves as a crown, bridge, denture or night guard. In between sit a dozen manual steps: monitoring scanner portals, retyping cases into lab software, checking scan quality, interpreting handwritten prescriptions, designing the restoration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We automate that pipeline. Our software connects to 15 intraoral scanner portals and more than five lab management systems, pulls cases the moment they arrive, reads the prescription, maps it into the lab&#39;s own product catalogue, checks the scan, and routes it to design. We serve roughly 6,000 customers across 28 countries from offices in Vancouver, Manila, Seoul and Shenzhen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The automation works. It does not yet work well enough, consistently enough, to run unattended — and closing that gap is the highest-leverage technical problem in the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish measurement.&lt;/strong&gt; Build per-model, per-customer, per-category accuracy reporting that Product and Sales can act on. Nothing else you do matters until this exists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the correction flywheel.&lt;/strong&gt; Capture the quality-control corrections our customers already make, turn them into structured, versioned training data, and close the loop with human review where confidence is low.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standardize the squads.&lt;/strong&gt; One deployment path, one evaluation harness, one model and dataset registry across restoration design, scan quality, prescription extraction and agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solve multi-tenant model behaviour.&lt;/strong&gt; Thousands of customer-specific product codes, prescription conventions and unwritten preferences sitting over a shared model base — without building a bespoke model per customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take inference to production scale.&lt;/strong&gt; Move workloads from on-premise to cloud with understood cost per inference and real concurrency headroom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• • &lt;strong&gt;Set technical direction for AI&lt;/strong&gt; across the company, partnering closely with the CTO, Product and the operations teams in Manila who currently absorb the work our models can&#39;t yet do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• • • • &lt;strong&gt;Before you apply — how we work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;This is a &lt;strong&gt;full-time in-office role at our Vancouver office, five days a week.&lt;/strong&gt; We are not offering remote or hybrid arrangements for this position, and this is not negotiable at offer stage.&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re explicit about it because the work genuinely depends on it. You&#39;ll be standardizing how four existing AI squads build, working across a Manila engineering organization, and spending real time with the operations people who currently absorb the work our models can&#39;t yet do. That happens in a room.&lt;br&gt;If you&#39;re looking for remote or hybrid, this isn&#39;t the right role and we&#39;d rather not waste your time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;br&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience building and operating &lt;strong&gt;machine learning platforms in production&lt;/strong&gt; — model registries, versioned datasets, CI for models, monitoring, rollback. Not research infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Depth in &lt;strong&gt;document and information extraction&lt;/strong&gt; from unstructured, inconsistent text. Prescriptions are the core data object here and they are messy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built a system where &lt;strong&gt;user corrections became better models&lt;/strong&gt;, and you can walk through exactly how the data moved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine &lt;strong&gt;evaluation rigour&lt;/strong&gt; — you can define what &quot;accurate&quot; means for a given category, defend it, and ship against it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Judgment about when not to use a model.&lt;/strong&gt; A significant share of this problem is classification and mapping, and deterministic rules beat ML for a lot of it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to &lt;strong&gt;align engineers across squads and time zones&lt;/strong&gt; without formal reporting authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strongly preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-tenant or per-customer model behaviour at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3D or geometry-based ML — directly relevant to scan quality and restoration design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with healthcare or other regulated data; patient privacy and data residency are live constraints for us.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inference cost management and on-premise to cloud migration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• • &lt;strong&gt;Not required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Dental or medical-device background. The workflow is learnable in an afternoon and we would rather have platform depth. What we do want is curiosity about a strange, physical, high-stakes manufacturing process — the output of our software ends up in someone&#39;s mouth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By 90 days&lt;/strong&gt; — you can tell us, with evidence, where our models actually fail and for which customers. The squads agree on a single evaluation standard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By six months&lt;/strong&gt; — customer corrections flow into training data automatically. At least one production model has measurably improved through that loop.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By twelve months&lt;/strong&gt; — prescription quality control runs with confidence thresholds, routing only genuinely ambiguous cases to human review. We can state our accuracy publicly and defend it in a sales conversation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Larger competitors have bigger AI teams and a five-year head start on modelling. We are not trying to beat them at that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are trying to build something they structurally cannot: a system that gets better every time one of six thousand laboratories tells us we got something wrong. That data exists. The loop does not.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have built this kind of flywheel before — or you have been close enough to one to know exactly why most of them fail — we should talk.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;3:1-3:52;82-133&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;On-site | Vancouver Office – &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;564 Beatty St&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our dentist business is being rebuilt, and we need someone who actually knows digital dentistry to stand beside our customers while we do it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Right now, dentists who send us digital cases are largely unsupported. There&#39;s no one dedicated to following up after a case comes in, answering design questions before they become problems, or helping a practice get more out of the platform. That work currently sits with one person who is also covering the lab side and simply doesn&#39;t have the hours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You would own it. You are the person a dentist talks to about their case — the one who understands what makes a case good, can say so plainly, and can push back when a clinician has it wrong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a design seat. You are not producing the cases yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talk to dentists.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Proactive follow-up after cases are submitted, consultation when they have questions, troubleshooting when something goes wrong.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Review cases.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Assess case quality and design architecture, and advise on how to get better outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow existing accounts.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Work with practices already sending to us on how to send more, and more of the right kind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feed the product.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Bring what you hear from dentists back to marketing, engineering, and product so the platform keeps improving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spot the advocates.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Identify customers who could become key opinion leaders for the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What success looks like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first 6–12 months, ranked:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Increase case volume from existing dentist customers by 25%&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build genuine working relationships across the customer base&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify and develop customer KOLs for the business&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll decide on your own&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own the day-to-day: who to call, what to escalate, what gets discussed with customers, and small refunds and credits. Larger refunds go to your manager. This role does not manage people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we need from you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on digital case design experience.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;You have designed in 3Shape and/or exocad, including complex cases, and you understand the architecture of what makes a case good.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ve consulted with dentists on their cases.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;You can hold your own in a clinical conversation — comfortable disagreeing with a dentist, and telling them clearly when a case won&#39;t work. Not easily intimidated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A strong, clear communicator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;You can describe a technical problem in a way anyone can act on, and people enjoy dealing with you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve carried revenue-linked KPIs before&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a known name in the digital dentistry industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Practical details&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hours&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Standard business hours, with flexibility for the occasional early or late call — including with our Manila team&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Setup&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;On-site&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Team size is still being scoped&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this seat exists&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;New role. The work is real and currently uncovered — Arnold is pulled in too many directions to do it full time&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product area&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Dentist-facing CAD design&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Data Architect - Hands-On Data Engineering &amp;amp; Architecture&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EviSmart | BGC, Taguig | Full-Time, Onsite&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;We need someone who can make our data trustworthy. And keep it that way.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At EviSmart, we&#39;re building AI-powered technology used by dental businesses across 28 countries. Our products are already live, and the data behind them directly affects how our teams operate, how our customers are served, and how our AI performs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Data Architect who can take ownership of that entire picture.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not someone who only creates architecture diagrams or delegates the difficult technical work. We need someone who can look at how data moves across our systems, question what isn&#39;t working, make better architectural decisions, and personally help implement the solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Someone who can lead engineers, challenge assumptions, and set the example through their own work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our data from source to consumption.&lt;/strong&gt; Understand how data is captured, ingested, transformed, stored, and made available to our teams and AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The reliability of our pipelines.&lt;/strong&gt; Improve existing ingestion processes, investigate failures, and build monitoring that catches problems before our users do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our data warehouse architecture.&lt;/strong&gt; Own data models, schemas, transformations, and the integrity of our Bronze, Silver, and Gold layers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data quality at its source.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify why records are missing, duplicated, inconsistent, or incorrect, and fix the underlying problem instead of repeatedly correcting reports.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integration across systems.&lt;/strong&gt; Help us establish consistent, reliable information across multiple data sources, including customer records and shared business entities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical direction and execution.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead a small data team, review architectural decisions, challenge weak solutions, and get hands-on when problems need solving.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong experience designing, building, and maintaining production data pipelines and data warehouses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on expertise in &lt;strong&gt;SQL, ETL/ELT, data modeling, and debugging production data issues&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with modern cloud data platforms, ideally &lt;strong&gt;Microsoft Azure, Azure Data Factory, Azure Data Lake, Databricks, or Microsoft Fabric&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Practical understanding of Medallion Architecture, data quality controls, monitoring, and pipeline reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience making architectural decisions, evaluating trade-offs, and leading technical implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to work with business stakeholders, challenge requirements, and translate problems into working technical solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Someone comfortable leading others while remaining actively involved in engineering.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Customer 360, Master Data Management, identity resolution, or event-driven data pipelines would be an advantage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What makes this role different?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re not coming in to build a data platform from zero.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We already have systems, pipelines, and an architecture in place. Your challenge is to understand what exists, identify where it falls short, improve it, and take responsibility for its reliability as we continue to grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with our technology leadership and a small engineering team, with the opportunity to influence decisions and see the direct impact of your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care less about how impressive your title sounds and more about &lt;strong&gt;what you&#39;ve personally built, the problems you&#39;ve challenged, and the outcomes you&#39;ve delivered.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Interested?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re the kind of engineer who enjoys understanding the whole problem, questioning the obvious solution, and getting into the details to make things work better, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Build reliable data. Lead by example. Own the outcome.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re not looking for developers who simply know how to code. We&#39;re looking for engineers who know how to figure out what needs to be built, why it matters, and how to make it work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can have 5, 10, or 15 years of experience with C#, .NET, React, and SQL. That&#39;s great. But experience alone won&#39;t qualify you for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What matters is what you can independently do with it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE&#39;RE BUILDING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EviSmart is building a dental Autopilot platform operating across 28 countries, supporting thousands of dental labs and dentists worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Manila engineering team builds and ships the systems that make this possible, including the application layer supporting our in-house AI development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These are real products, serving real customers, with real operational consequences when something doesn&#39;t work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re hiring engineers who can take responsibility for that.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE ACTUALLY EXPECT YOU TO DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Figure out the problem before writing code.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You won&#39;t always receive perfectly documented requirements or detailed instructions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You need to be comfortable talking to stakeholders, understanding how the business works, identifying what&#39;s actually broken, and translating that into a technical solution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That means doing business analysis when necessary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not because you&#39;re replacing a Business Analyst, but because &lt;strong&gt;you cannot build the right solution if you don&#39;t understand the problem.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Build it yourself. From the ground up.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We need engineers who can personally develop substantial features across:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;C# / .NET Core&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ReactJS / JavaScript&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SQL Server&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;REST APIs and system integrations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should be capable of working across the frontend, backend, and database without depending on another developer to figure out the difficult parts for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re not hiring someone whose primary contribution is researching technologies, recommending frameworks, or delegating the actual development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You need to be able to execute.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Challenge requirements when they don&#39;t make sense.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A requirement isn&#39;t automatically the right solution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you see a better approach, explain it. If something creates unnecessary complexity, challenge it. If a proposed solution solves the wrong problem, say so.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect you to understand trade-offs, ask difficult questions, and propose alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We value engineers who think, not just engineers who agree.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Solve problems without waiting to be told every step.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll encounter unfamiliar systems, incomplete information, technical constraints, and things that don&#39;t work the first time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your responsibility is to investigate, understand, experiment, and find a way forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ask for help when necessary. Collaborate with the team. Escalate genuine risks early.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But don&#39;t confuse collaboration with waiting for someone else to solve the problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Own what happens after you build it.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Writing code isn&#39;t the finish line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You need to test your work, validate business requirements, investigate failures, and ensure the feature is actually ready for production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If it breaks, you help fix it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If it doesn&#39;t solve the original problem, you&#39;re not done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If there&#39;s a risk to delivery, you raise it early.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibility isn&#39;t just to complete a ticket. It&#39;s to deliver something that works.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE TECHNICAL FOUNDATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should already have substantial hands-on experience with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;C# / ASP.NET Core / .NET&lt;/strong&gt; — building production backend services and business logic&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ReactJS&lt;/strong&gt; — personally developing production web applications, not just listing it on your CV&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SQL Server&lt;/strong&gt; — designing schemas, writing queries, investigating performance, and understanding data integrity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REST APIs&lt;/strong&gt; — designing, building, integrating, and troubleshooting services&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-end delivery&lt;/strong&gt; — taking features from problem discovery through development, testing, and production readiness&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Azure, CI/CD, automated testing, and AI-assisted development tools is valuable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But tools don&#39;t replace engineering judgment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WILL STRUGGLE HERE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is probably not for you if:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You prefer receiving detailed tickets and implementing exactly what&#39;s written.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You need someone else to define the technical solution before you can begin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your experience is primarily coordinating developers rather than personally building software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You avoid questioning requirements, even when you see a problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You consider a feature finished once the code compiles or the ticket is closed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You expect seniority, years of experience, or job titles to speak for your capability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your main priority is securing a higher salary without taking on the accountability that comes with it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There&#39;s nothing wrong with preferring a more structured development environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This just isn&#39;t that environment.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WILL THRIVE HERE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll likely enjoy this role if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Get curious about the business problem before discussing technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enjoy building systems from scratch and figuring things out independently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Can move comfortably between frontend, backend, APIs, and databases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Take pride in solving problems other people haven&#39;t figured out yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Speak up when you disagree and can explain why.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Care whether your solution actually improves something.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want your compensation and career growth to reflect the value you consistently deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t expect you to know everything.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We expect you to know how to figure things out — and have the ability to execute once you do.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply at&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/evismart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EviSmart • Philippines • evismart.com&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BGC, Taguig • 100% Onsite • Full-Time&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;On-site | Vancouver Office – 564 Beatty St&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Problem You&#39;ll Solve&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EviSmart builds software and AI-powered solutions for dental labs and dentists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dental workflows depend on information: where each case is, what was requested, what&#39;s due next, and what needs attention. Today, that information is often scattered across different systems, spreadsheets, emails, and phone calls. This makes it difficult for teams to see what&#39;s happening and act quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building a family of &lt;strong&gt;Command Centers&lt;/strong&gt; to change that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each Command Center brings important information and workflows into one place, helping teams manage everything from 3D scans and dental designs to case intake and follow-ups. AI helps automate routine tasks, giving people more time to focus on decisions and customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Junior Full-Stack Developer who wants to help build these products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work alongside experienced engineers, contribute to features that solve real problems, and gain hands-on experience across frontend, backend, and 3D development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value curiosity, accountability, and people who take pride in their work. You won&#39;t be expected to know everything, but we do expect you to think critically, ask questions, and take responsibility for the quality of what you build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build features that matter.&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to our Command Centers, from frontend interfaces to backend logic. You&#39;ll help understand the problem, write code, test your work, and improve it based on feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investigate and solve problems.&lt;/strong&gt; Debug issues, trace them to their root cause, and work with teammates to find solutions that prevent the same problems from happening again.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work with 3D technology.&lt;/strong&gt; Help build and improve browser-based tools that allow users to view and interact with 3D dental scans and designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work with data.&lt;/strong&gt; Write logic to retrieve, structure, clean, and combine information from different sources, keeping performance and reliability in mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use AI to build smarter.&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI coding tools to accelerate development while understanding, reviewing, and testing the code they produce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate and challenge ideas.&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with engineers, designers, and product managers. Ask questions, share ideas, and speak up when you see opportunities to improve something.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take ownership of your work.&lt;/strong&gt; Follow through on commitments, communicate when you&#39;re stuck, and care about what happens to your code after it ships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1–2 years of professional software development experience&lt;/strong&gt;, with exposure to both frontend and backend development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend development experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience building web applications using JavaScript or TypeScript and a modern framework such as React, Angular, or Vue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend development experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with server-side programming, APIs, and backend languages such as C#, Java, Python, or JavaScript/TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Database fundamentals.&lt;/strong&gt; Working knowledge of SQL or NoSQL databases, including how to retrieve, organize, and update data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Debugging and testing skills.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience investigating software issues, using version control such as Git, and writing basic tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with AI coding tools.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve used tools such as Claude Code, Cursor, or GitHub Copilot and can explain, review, and validate the code they generate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A strong sense of ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; You take responsibility for your work, follow through on commitments, and care about getting things right.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curiosity and a willingness to learn.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re comfortable asking questions, receiving feedback, and working through unfamiliar challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logical problem-solving skills.&lt;/strong&gt; You can break down problems, explain your reasoning, and approach debugging methodically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;C#/.NET, or Microsoft Azure&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;3D technologies&lt;/strong&gt; such as Three.js, WebGL, Babylon.js, Unity, or Unreal Engine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI-powered applications or integrating LLMs into software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI agents, prompt engineering, or AI-driven workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a startup, small product team, or fast-paced development environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;Apply today @ &lt;a href=&quot;https://evismart.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Evismart Careers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evident | Nimbyx Group of Companies • BGC, Taguig | Fully Onsite&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Head of Finance&lt;/strong&gt; to lead our Philippine finance operations and ensure our accounting, reporting, and regulatory compliance are accurate, efficient, and well-managed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role. You&#39;ll oversee the local finance team, take ownership of our Philippine financial operations, and work closely with our Canada Finance team and Manila leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who doesn&#39;t just manage financial processes but knows how to improve them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accounting &amp;amp; Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Own month-end closing, financial statements, reconciliations, and general ledger accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tax &amp;amp; Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure timely BIR, SEC, and other government filings, including statutory audits and payroll-related remittances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cash Flow &amp;amp; Budgeting:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage cash flow, banking, payables, budgeting, forecasting, and financial reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal Controls:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish and improve financial processes, approval controls, and compliance procedures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead and develop the Manila finance team, ensuring accountability and consistent performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate with Canada Finance on intercompany transactions, financial reporting, and group accounting standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Licensed CPA in the Philippines (required).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At least &lt;strong&gt;8 years of experience&lt;/strong&gt; in finance and accounting, including &lt;strong&gt;3 years in a leadership role&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong knowledge of Philippine taxation, statutory compliance, and IFRS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience managing month-end closing and financial reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with intercompany accounting and reporting to an international or foreign parent company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong Excel, analytical, and financial management skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent communication skills and the ability to work with senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Willing to work fully onsite in BGC, Taguig, with some working-hour overlap with Canada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Will Make You Successful&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You take ownership of financial accuracy and compliance, identify problems before they escalate, and continuously look for ways to improve processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can lead a team while staying close enough to the details to know when something isn&#39;t right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you can own the numbers, strengthen the controls, and turn financial information into better business decisions, we&#39;d like to hear from you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;job-sections&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;section id=&quot;st-companyDescription&quot; class=&quot;job-section&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-sections&quot;&gt;
&lt;section id=&quot;st-qualifications&quot; class=&quot;job-section&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;wysiwyg spl-wysiwyg&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Product Support Specialist&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EviSmart | Global Continuity Team • On-site • Full-Time • Night Shift&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Product Support Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; who can help customers resolve software issues and keep their operations running.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers are dental labs and dentists around the world who rely on our software every day. When something isn&#39;t working, we need someone who can understand the problem, find a practical solution, and keep the customer informed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assist customers with software issues, questions, and troubleshooting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understand how our products work and how customers use them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find temporary workarounds when an immediate fix isn&#39;t available.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage support tickets and follow through until issues are resolved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with Technical Support and Engineering teams on more complex issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide clear and timely updates to customers during incidents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify recurring problems and help prevent them from happening again.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help improve our support processes and knowledge resources.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in software product support, application support, or SaaS customer support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to troubleshoot software issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Good written and verbal English communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to explain technical problems in simple terms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with ticketing systems and basic technical troubleshooting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to prioritize issues and remain calm under pressure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A proactive mindset and willingness to learn complex software products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You don&#39;t need to be a software developer.&lt;/strong&gt; What matters is your ability to understand the product, solve customer problems, and take ownership until customers can continue working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About EviSmart&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EviSmart develops software that helps dental labs and dental professionals manage their digital workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join our Global Continuity team, working alongside Product Support and Technical Support Specialists to help customers around the world keep their operations running.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interested? Apply now and join our team.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Can you keep customers moving when the product doesn’t?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Product Support Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; who can do more than answer questions. You’ll need to understand the product, troubleshoot problems, find workarounds fast, and keep customers informed when things go wrong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With AI handling the straightforward questions, you’ll take on the challenges that require human judgment, resourcefulness, and ownership. When an issue needs deeper technical expertise, you’ll work with our Technical Support Specialists to get to the bottom of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think you can solve problems before they become disruptions?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;3:1-3:52;82-133&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;On-site | Vancouver Office – &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;564 Beatty St&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Our Mission&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;9:1-9:60;156-215&quot;&gt;Our mission is to amplify human success with AI automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;11:1-11:265;217-481&quot;&gt;In a dental lab, that means technicians spend less time on repetitive casework and more on the complex cases that need real skill, and labs take on volume they used to turn away. We automate the parts of the job nobody wants.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;13:1-13:127;483-609&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our vision is to become the operating system of the dental industry.&lt;/em&gt; Not a tool a lab logs into. The system a lab runs on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Problem We&#39;re Solving&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;21:1-23:16;620-832&quot;&gt;A dental lab loses hours every week to a question that shouldn&#39;t need asking: &lt;em&gt;where is that case?&lt;/em&gt; Orders arrive from a dozen different manufacturer portals, and chasing them down has always been somebody&#39;s job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;25:1-27:54;834-1088&quot;&gt;The Command Center ends that. It gives a lab full visibility of every case — what arrived, what stage it&#39;s at, what&#39;s stuck and why — updating continuously, in one place. Your job is to build the next generation of it around the way a lab actually works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;19:1-19:16;886-901&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why EviSmart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;21:1-24:88;903-1175&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;21:1-21:60;903-962&quot;&gt;300 people. Two hubs: Vancouver HQ and Manila operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;22:1-22:62;963-1024&quot;&gt;145% year-over-year SaaS growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;23:1-23:63;1025-1087&quot;&gt;28 countries. One platform. The dental industry&#39;s operating system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;24:1-24:88;1088-1175&quot;&gt;An in-house AI model research and development team building proprietary intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role Exists&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;28:1-28:511;1202-1712&quot;&gt;A lab isn&#39;t one job. It&#39;s designers, technicians, quality control, case managers, shipping, the owner — each with a different week and a different definition of what matters today. Full visibility means something different to each of them. The next generation of Command Centers has to be built around how those roles actually work. No written definition exists yet of what the next version of the Command Center must contain, what&#39;s optional, or what disqualifies one from shipping.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;You write that definition, and you write it from inside dental labs. Then you hold it, while everything else gets built against it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;34:1-41:158;1764-3244&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;35:1-35:135;1842-1976&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build from what you see: &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ll be in dental labs - interviewing and standing next to the end users while they work. We know these workflows, 2,000+ lab customers. What no one has at the fidelity a per-role surface needs is the detail: a designer&#39;s week is not an operations manager&#39;s, and full visibility means something different to each of them.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;35:1-35:135;1842-1976&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define the Command Center spec.&lt;/strong&gt; What every Command Center must contain, what&#39;s optional, what stops one shipping.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;35:1-35:135;1842-1976&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the failure states.&lt;/strong&gt; A lab can only promise a date if we know the case is actually moving. Automation can stop without announcing it. Staleness and last-successful-sync, exception queues, splitting failures by cause, confidence thresholds, when a case routes to a person and how — all of it exists so the date we gave a lab stays true, or so they hear about it early enough to act.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;35:1-35:135;1842-1976&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get the measurement live.&lt;/strong&gt; The number this role is measured on is Weekly Active Role-Fit: the share of the lab roles a Command Center is built for who open it in a normal week. The bar is 80% on pilots. Building the tracking is on you, and baselines get captured before launch, not after.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;35:1-35:135;1842-1976&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Document the decisions.&lt;/strong&gt; The problem statement, the acceptance criteria, what was decided and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
